TASK: Redesign and restructure Writing Mode on iOS into a clean chat-based writing experience.

CURRENT PROBLEM:
The current Writing Mode screen is too complex and crowded.
It currently looks like a dashboard with:
- large Writing Mode title
- long description
- oversized prompt box
- writing category cards
- Personal Writing Style card
- multiple large sections

This makes the screen feel cluttered and unlike the rest of BlueMind.

GOAL:
Writing Mode should feel like a NORMAL BlueMind chat screen, but with specialized writing capabilities.

Think:
“Normal Chat + Writing Intelligence”

Do NOT make it look like a dashboard.

==================================================
1. CORE SCREEN STRUCTURE
==================================================

Rebuild the Writing Mode screen using the SAME general layout structure as the normal BlueMind Chat screen.

Top:
- normal iOS/BlueMind header
- title: Writing Mode
- writing pen icon
- optional compact writing-type selector

Middle:
- normal conversation area
- user messages
- AI responses
- scrolling conversation

Bottom:
- normal BlueMind chat composer
- attachment +
- text input
- microphone
- send button

The user should immediately understand how to use it because it behaves like Chat.

==================================================
2. HEADER
==================================================

Use the same header proportions and spacing as the normal Chat screen.

Do NOT use the current oversized:
“WRITING MODE”
“Writing Mode”
large description block.

Instead:

Title:
Writing Mode

Optional subtitle should be minimal or omitted.

Use the existing BlueMind iOS glass header controls.

If back/menu behavior already exists in normal Chat, reuse it.

Do not invent a separate navigation system.

==================================================
3. WRITING TYPE SELECTOR
==================================================

Writing Mode needs special writing categories, but they must NOT occupy a large horizontal dashboard section.

Supported types can include existing categories:
- Email
- Report
- Essay
- Story
- Professional writing
- Other

Preferred UX:
Use one compact selector in or under the header.

Example:
[ Email ▾ ]

Tapping it should open a native-style iOS selection sheet/menu.

The menu can show:
- Email
- Report
- Essay
- Story
- Professional
- Other

When selected:
- update the current writing mode
- AI should use the selected type as context
- close the sheet

Do NOT show all categories permanently across the page.

==================================================
4. CHAT EXPERIENCE
==================================================

The actual Writing Mode should behave like a specialized chat.

Example:

User:
“Write an email to my teacher saying I will miss class tomorrow.”

AI:
generates the email.

Then user can continue naturally:
“Make it shorter.”
“Make it more formal.”
“Translate it to Swedish.”

Conversation must persist like a normal chat where appropriate.

Do not force the user through forms for every writing task.

==================================================
5. WRITING-SPECIFIC AI CONTEXT
==================================================

The Writing Mode AI should know:

- selected writing type
- current conversation context
- user's Personal Writing Style if enabled
- requested tone/language
- previous edits in the same conversation

Do not send unnecessary UI state to the model.

Use the existing backend/AI architecture where possible.

==================================================
6. RESPONSE ACTIONS
==================================================

Writing Mode should have useful writing actions directly under AI-generated text.

After a writing response, show compact actions such as:

- Improve
- Shorter
- Longer
- Professional
- Simpler
- Rewrite
- Translate

Use compact Apple/BlueMind glass controls.

Do NOT use giant cards.

These actions should act on the relevant generated text.

Example:
Press “Shorter”
-> ask the writing AI to shorten the current answer.

Press “Professional”
-> rewrite the same content professionally.

==================================================
7. PERSONAL WRITING STYLE
==================================================

The current large “Personal Writing Style” card should be removed from the main screen.

Do NOT delete the feature.

Move it into a compact Writing Tools / settings control.

Possible placement:
- small pen/settings icon in header
- or inside writing type menu
- or a compact “Writing Style” action

When opened:
show a native-style iOS sheet.

The sheet can allow:
- view current writing style
- create style
- edit style
- enable/disable style

Do not keep the current huge card visible all the time.

==================================================
8. PERSONAL STYLE BEHAVIOR
==================================================

If Personal Writing Style is enabled:
Writing Mode should automatically use it when generating content.

The user should NOT need to select it every time.

If disabled:
use normal BlueMind writing behavior.

Preserve existing saved style data.

Do not wipe or recreate user style records unnecessarily.

==================================================
9. COMPOSER
==================================================

Reuse the SAME composer architecture as Normal Chat.

Expected structure:

[ + ] [ Ask BlueMind to write... ] [ mic ] [ send ]

or preserve existing placeholder if there is already a global composer system.

Do NOT use the current giant writing prompt box.

The composer should:
- grow naturally for multiline text
- handle keyboard safely
- respect iOS safe area
- not overlap content
- use current Apple/BlueMind glass style

==================================================
10. PLACEHOLDER
==================================================

Use a writing-specific placeholder, for example:

“Ask BlueMind to write...”

or:
“What would you like to write?”

Keep it short.

Do not use a huge instructional paragraph.

==================================================
11. EMPTY STATE
==================================================

When there are no messages yet, show a clean lightweight empty state.

Example:

Writing Mode
“Write, rewrite, improve, or translate anything.”

Optional compact suggestion chips:
- Write an email
- Improve text
- Rewrite professionally
- Translate

Do not turn this into a large dashboard.

Once conversation begins, the suggestions should disappear.

==================================================
12. IOS / APPLE GLASS
==================================================

Use the existing BlueMind iOS glass system.

Apply it to:
- header buttons
- writing type selector
- Writing Tools
- composer buttons
- response actions
- native sheets/menus

Do NOT create a new fake CSS glass system.

Reuse existing native-backed components where available.

==================================================
13. WRITING TYPE SHEET
==================================================

The type selector should use a compact iOS-style sheet/menu.

Do not create a giant custom panel.

Use:
- native-like spacing
- clean rows
- selected checkmark
- correct dismissal behavior

==================================================
14. WRITING TOOLS SHEET
==================================================

Add a compact Writing Tools sheet/menu if needed.

Potential actions:
- Personal Writing Style
- Change writing type
- Tone
- Language
- Start new writing chat

Keep this lightweight.

Do not overload it with unrelated settings.

==================================================
15. TONE
==================================================

If tone control already exists or is appropriate, support compact tone options such as:

- Neutral
- Professional
- Friendly
- Formal
- Casual

Tone should be optional.

Do not force the user to choose before writing.

==================================================
16. LANGUAGE
==================================================

Writing Mode should support multilingual writing naturally.

At minimum:
- English
- Arabic
- Swedish
- mixed-language prompts

Do not break RTL Arabic layout.

AI should infer language by default unless user explicitly chooses another language.

==================================================
17. NORMAL CHAT VS WRITING MODE
==================================================

Do NOT merge the two features.

Normal Chat remains Normal Chat.

Writing Mode uses the same UI structure but different AI behavior and writing tools.

Visually:
similar architecture

Functionally:
Writing Mode is specialized for writing.

==================================================
18. DO NOT TOUCH
==================================================

Do NOT modify:
- Projects
- AI Plans
- Search
- Hidden Chat
- Private Chat
- Face ID
- Schedule
- Reminders
- unrelated Settings
- normal Chat behavior

Only reuse shared Chat components where necessary.

==================================================
19. STATE AND NAVIGATION
==================================================

When leaving Writing Mode and returning:
preserve the current writing conversation where appropriate.

Do not reset the Writing Mode screen unnecessarily.

Do not trigger app restart.

Do not trigger Face ID again unless the global security policy requires it.

==================================================
20. KEYBOARD
==================================================

Test keyboard behavior carefully.

When keyboard opens:
- composer sits directly above keyboard
- no duplicate input bars
- no overlap
- conversation remains scrollable
- last message remains reachable

When keyboard closes:
layout returns smoothly.

==================================================
21. RESPONSE EDITING FLOW
==================================================

When the user selects:
Improve
Shorter
Longer
Professional
Simpler
Rewrite
Translate

Apply the action to the correct most recent writing output.

Do not create disconnected random responses.

Maintain context.

==================================================
22. BACKEND / AI LOGIC
==================================================

Inspect existing Writing Mode backend/AI logic before adding new code.

Reuse:
- current AI provider
- current chat/session architecture
- saved writing style
- auth/session handling

Avoid duplicate AI pipelines.

If Writing Mode currently uses a different prompt builder, preserve its useful logic but connect it to the new chat-based UI.

==================================================
23. PERSISTENCE
==================================================

If Writing Mode conversations are intended to persist:
ensure they save and reload correctly.

If they use the existing chat model:
reuse it with a writing-mode flag/type.

Do not create an unnecessary parallel database system.

==================================================
